# =============================================================================
# .gitignore
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS HERE: `git ls-files` currently reports 20060 tracked files,
# 13137 of them under reports/ -- about 620 MB of Vivado logs already committed.
# Adding a path here does NOT untrack a file that is already in the index, so
# this file only stops the bleeding. See "already tracked" at the bottom.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Vivado scratch ---------------------------------------------------------
.Xil/
*.jou
*.str
usage_statistics_webtalk*
vivado_pid*
vivado*.backup.log
hs_err_pid*.log
.Xil
vivado_projects/

# ---- Xilinx simulator (xvlog / xelab / xsim) --------------------------------
xsim.dir/
xelab.pb
xvlog.pb
xsim.log
webtalk*.log
*.wdb
*.vcd
*.saif

# ---- Icarus Verilog ---------------------------------------------------------
*.vvp
sim.out

# ---- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# ---- sweep and driver output ------------------------------------------------
# reports/ holds the NSGA-II sweep's per-design CSVs (3.3 MB, worth keeping) and
# its per-design Vivado logs (620 MB, regenerable). Ignore the logs, keep the
# CSVs -- the CSVs are the provenance for the published numbers.
reports/*.log
optimization.log
generation.txt
sweep*.log
sweep.pid
smoke*.log
*_saif.log
*_pwr.log

# Driver scratch: staged sources, per-design Vivado logs, funcsim netlists.
# The committed record is the report .txt and the metrics .csv, not the workdirs.
#
# Every directory a driver writes per-probe or per-design scratch into belongs
# here. constraint_sweep/ was the gap that let Vivado logs and staged copies of
# verilog_sources into the index, where they then produced merge conflicts
# between the two machines.
**/fpga_work/
**/fpga_work_impl/
**/synth_work/
synth_mixed/fpga_work*/
synth_mixed/constraint_sweep/
synth_mixed/soc_fpga_work*/
sim_soc_perf/
sim/

# Run logs are per-machine and per-run. They are tracked, because the whole
# point is to read digital-1's results from anywhere -- but the filename carries
# the hostname, so two machines never write the same path and can never conflict.
# These bare names are the pre-hostname ones and are no longer produced:
synth_mixed/three_way_comparison.log
synth_mixed/mixed_fpga_report.log
synth_mixed/closing_period.log
synth_mixed/implementation_delta.log
synth_mixed/soc_throughput.log
synth_mixed/soc_fpga_report.log
fp16_baseline/synth/fp16_fpga_report.log
fp32_baseline/synth/fp32_fpga_report.log

# ---- generated RTL ----------------------------------------------------------
# generated_designs/ accumulates one file per evaluation (4227 of them) and is
# regenerable from a chromosome plus fft_template_generator.py in one command.
#
# generated_cores_gated/ is deliberately NOT ignored: those 18 files are the
# exact RTL the published FPGA numbers were measured on, they are small, and
# keeping them means the measured designs can be re-synthesised without first
# re-deriving the chromosome selection.
generated_designs/

# ---- archives and attic -----------------------------------------------------
*.zip
*.tar.gz
_attic/

# ---- OS ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# =============================================================================
# ALREADY TRACKED -- this file cannot help with those. To stop carrying them
# without touching the working tree or losing any file on disk:
#
#   git rm -r --cached reports .Xil generated_designs vivado_projects
#   git commit -m "stop tracking Vivado logs and generated RTL"
#
# Then re-add just the CSVs that are the sweep's provenance:
#
#   git add -f reports/*.csv
#   git commit -m "keep per-design metrics CSVs"
#
# That removes ~620 MB from future commits. It does NOT shrink .git, because the
# blobs stay in history; only a history rewrite (git filter-repo / BFG) does
# that, and it rewrites every commit hash, so every existing clone -- digital-1
# included -- has to be re-cloned. Decide that separately.
# =============================================================================
